.TH GIT-SQ 1 2026-09-24 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-sq \- interactively squash the current branch's own commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git sq
.RI [ base ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run
.B git rebase \-i \-\-keep\-base
against
.IR base :
by default the remote copy of the dev branch, or of the main branch for
hotfix branches. Only this branch's commits are rewritten; the branch is
never moved onto a newer base (that is what
.BR git\-sync (1)
is for), so a squash can't turn into a surprise conflict.
.PP
Rewriting a protected branch warns first, or stops when
.B workflow.strict
is true. If the squashed commits had been pushed, it says to publish with
.BR "git ps force" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-ps (1),
.BR git\-workflow (7)
